      "notes": "One validator with the 3-of-4 BLS sharing from bls_threshold.json. signature_aggregate is a plain aggregate of the lock hash signed by all four private shares, and charon's VerifyAggregate accepts it against the four public shares. node_signatures are secp256k1 signatures of the same lock hash by each operator's node key, and each operator's ENR really carries that key, so charon verifies them from the ENRs alone. node_pubkeys repeats those keys so an implementation that does not decode ENRs can still check the signatures. The operator and creator EIP-712 signatures are placeholder bytes: they are covered by the hashes but charon's signing helpers for them are not exported."
